{"slug": "americas-most-innovative-companies", "title": "America's Most Innovative Companies", "year": 2025, "rank": 115, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "worlds-most-admired-companies", "title": "World's Most Admired Companies", "year": 2025, "rank": null, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "fortune500--technology", "title": "Fortune Sector Leaders: Technology", "year": 2024, "rank": 38, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "fortune500", "title": "Fortune 500", "year": 2024, "rank": 396, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "americas-most-innovative-companies", "title": "America's Most Innovative Companies", "year": 2024, "rank": 170, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "worlds-most-admired-companies", "title": "World's Most Admired Companies", "year": 2024, "rank": null, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "future", "title": "The Future 50", "year": 2023, "rank": 35, "itemDescription": "The online hospitality network recovered from the pandemic travel slump with lightning speed: It cracked the Fortune 500 list of top companies by revenue for the first time in 2023, and analysts expect the company to grow revenue by 17% in 2023, to $9.8 billion, and by another 12% in 2024. Concerns over a possible inflation-driven travel slowdown put Airbnb\u2019s share price on a yo-yo trajectory for most of 2023, but more bullish investors have applauded the company\u2019s efforts to boost its inventory of less-expensive listings, and its potential to use AI to protect its profit margins."}, {"slug": "fortune500", "title": "Fortune 500", "year": 2023, "rank": 450, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "fortune500", "title": "Fortune 500", "year": 2022, "rank": 528, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "future", "title": "The Future 50", "year": 2021, "rank": 5, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "change-the-world", "title": "Change the World", "year": 2021, "rank": 16, "itemDescription": "<span style=\"font-weight: 400\">Since Hurricane Sandy struck in 2012, Airbnb has helped organize temporary housing for refugees, asylum seekers, and people displaced by disaster; it has served 75,000 people so far. In August, as Afghanistan fell to the Taliban, Airbnb\u2019s nonprofit arm said it would pay for hosts to house 20,000 Afghans. In September, Airbnb said that support from the host community had helped exceed that goal.</span>"}, {"slug": "fortune500", "title": "Fortune 500", "year": 2021, "rank": 688, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "change-the-world", "title": "Change the World", "year": 2017, "rank": 31, "itemDescription": ""}]}